MID_SCXX_05_01_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_001: Now then, thank you for coming! Allow me to\nexplain the nature of the predicament before us.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_002: I've lost some magic cannonballs, manufactured\nin the arcane city of Morfis.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_003: The missing cargo also includes quite a robust\ncollection of very powerful, very exclusive weapons.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_004: A bunch of powerful weapons? Why would you have\nstuff like that?
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_005: Things are not as they should be. How exciting.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_006: You were trading in these? You must know that\nsmuggling weapons into the capital is prohibited.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_007: 
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_008: 
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_009: 
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_010: Whoa-ho! Sorry, but that's all the cards I can show\nfor now. But I can promise these aren't for violence.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_011: Now, if your reservations have been alleviated, back\nto the missing carriage... Ursula?
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_012: Yes. After receiving the cargo from the Port of\nPandora, the carriage began a journey south...
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_013: The plan was to start at Aesobos and travel to\nDagsion through Dragdon Pass...
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_014: We meant to take the cargo off their hands once they\ncleared the pass, but they never showed.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_015: It's almost as if they just...
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_016: And that is where we are, people! Lost merchandise,\ncryptic vanishings. Come, I'll show you the way.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_017: Over there!
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_018: The carriage is totally destroyed.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_019: That's the carriage. The damage is...unusual.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_020: Is that the Vandahl Trading Company carriage?\nSomeone has thoroughly destroyed it.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_021: 
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_022: 
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_023: 
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_024: Damn, I thought this might be the case. But no sign\nof the cargo. Hmm... Perhaps it was taken?
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_025: These marks on the sides here. It's almost as if the\ncarriage was torn apart.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_026: Yes... But this doesn't look like the work of men.\nThis was something far more...primal.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_027: Eugh. What in the—
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_028: Talimun, I think it's threatening us. It seems we've\nstumbled into its territory.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_029: And it thinks everything, even the carriage, belongs\nto it now.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_030: So a bird was the culprit the whole time, huh?
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_031: Ursula. I'll leave the carriage to you. Recover what\nyou can and get it out of here.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_032: I'll see it done.
MID_SCXX_05_01_m01_033: Meanwhile, we'll make for the nest! We're getting\nthat cargo back!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_001: Damn! Turns out there's tons of these blasted things.\nThis is going to be a pain...
MID_SCXX_05_02_m16: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_002: One of 'em's carrying something big. Are the\nweapons inside it?
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_003: Is that the one you're after? It looks conspicuous.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_004: One of them carries a heavy load. Might your magic\ncannonballs be inside?
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_005: 
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_006: 
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_007: 
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_008: Yeah, I think you're right! Let's take it down quick\nand be done with it, shall we?
MID_SCXX_05_02_m17: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_009: HA! What luck! These fools left their treasure\neverywhere. Grab as much as you can carry, men!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_010: Oh, come on! OK, new plan. We teach these thieves\nto keep their hands to themselves!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_011: We can't let them steal the weapons. We have to\nget them back.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_012: None will remain standing.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_013: They will fall as easily as the birds do. I shall crush\nthem between my fingers like insects.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_014: 
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_015: 
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_016: 
MID_SCXX_05_02_m01_017: Thieves, birds, and {SetColor=Gold}recapturing our cargo{SetColor=Default}. Looks like\nwe have our work cut out for us.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m02: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m02_001: No! They got away!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m02_002: I can't catch up with them!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m02_003: They're gone, and with them, my chance.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m02_004: Rrgh. I did not credit them with such guile. It would\nbe a different story if we were at sea.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m02_005: 
MID_SCXX_05_02_m02_006: 
MID_SCXX_05_02_m02_007: 
MID_SCXX_05_02_m02_008: Now, how the hell could I have screwed this up?!\nGrr... What a bust...
MID_SCXX_05_02_m03: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m03_001: Hey, Cai! You give it your all, and I might just treat\nyou with a reward, OK?
MID_SCXX_05_02_m03_002: Don't treat me like a kid. I was trying to help you,\nold man.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m03_003: Hehehe. Someone's touchy. Well, thanks anyway.\nI'm relying on you!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m04: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m04_001: Hey, Dietrich. Please do mind the cargo. Wouldn't\nwant you chopping IT to pieces too.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m04_002: If you wish it unscathed, then you must be the one to\nprotect it.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m04_003: Yeesh. Not the most personable guy around, is he?\nEven so, can't deny the man's skill!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m05: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m05_001: I worry for the future of our alliance if these common\nhoodlums are giving you trouble.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m05_002: I'm no stranger to trouble, Majesty. It's overcoming it\nthat shows the true measure of a merchant, you see.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m05_003: Tch! Then show me how you would be measured.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m06: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m06_001: This is turning out to be more trouble than I\nexpected. But I said I would help you, and I will.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m06_002: Then I appreciate your commitment, my friend!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m07: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m07_001: You know, we're the ones at fault. We've all entered\nthe birds' territory. We should apologize.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m07_002: You've got a point. If they don't kill us first, perhaps\ntaming them could be useful for the company?
MID_SCXX_05_02_m08: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m08_001: It strikes me that this bird is large enough for many\nuses. Food, clothing...
MID_SCXX_05_02_m08_002: Oho! So it turns out the bride has the eye of a\nmerchant, eh? Seeing the value in everything is key.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m09: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m09_001: Oh, Simon! Boy, am I glad to see you. Ready\nto work?
MID_SCXX_05_02_m09_002: Aren't I always? Point me where you need, and I'll\nget the job done!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m10: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m10_001: No half measures, Ludia! Remember, here at\nVandahl Trading, we only deal in excellence!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m10_002: Yes, sir! Everyone knows organization and focus\nis key for any merchant, sir! 
MID_SCXX_05_02_m10_003: Hahaha. That's right, but... Hey! Was that a\njab at me?
MID_SCXX_05_02_m11: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m11_001: Hey, Fianna, Centurio might worry, but I know you\ncan handle yourself. I'm counting on you to, anyway.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m11_002: OK! If you mean that...I'll do my best!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m12: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m12_001: Sorry, friend, but that cargo belongs to the Vandahl\nTrading Company! I'll be taking it back now.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m13: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m13_001: Alright! Got the goods!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m13_002: HEY! Put that down you— Grrr. Fine! I'll just have\nto {SetColor=Gold}get it back before they can escape{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m14: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m14_001: OK, that's one accounted for. Now to collect the rest!
MID_SCXX_05_02_m15: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_02_m15_001: We've got it all! Well, no point in hanging\naround here.
MID_SCXX_05_02_m15_002: Let's go before someone from the temples hears the\ncommotion and comes running.
MID_SCXX_05_e10: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_e10_001: Nice, it's dropped the cargo! We should grab it\nwhile we can!
MID_SCXX_05_e11: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_e11_001: Damn it, that's my property! Keep your grubby\nhands—ah, talons off of it.
MID_SCXX_05_e11_002: Not so easy to fly while carrying something heavy,\nis it? Well then, drop it already!
MID_SCXX_05_e12: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_e12_001: Who are these guys and why do they keep getting\nin our way?!
MID_SCXX_05_e13: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_e13_001: Everyone, leave the birds for now. Focus your energy\non the fools on the ground first!
MID_SCXX_05_e13_002: Looks like they're turning their attention on us!\nCareful, everyone!
MID_SCXX_05_e16: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_e16_001: And of course. The birds see us as the problem now.\nAlright, come on, then!
MID_SCXX_05_e17: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_e17_001: Watch your heads!
MID_SCXX_05_e18: <TH>
MID_SCXX_05_e18_001: With the birds and bandits fighting each other, it\nshould make it that much easier to get my stuff back.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_001: OK! Ran into some trouble along the way, but I'd say\neverything worked out in the end. Thanks for that.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_002: Hey, one of the packages looks different from\nthe others.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_003: Hm? This package seems different.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_004: Odd. One of these packages bears a different insignia\nfrom the rest.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_005: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_006: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_007: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_008: Hm? Ah, yeah, you're right. This isn't one of Vandahl\nTrading's. This must've belonged to the bandits.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_009: Well, would you look at that. It's sent from one of\nour rivals, actually. Mandalan Trading.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_010: But sent to who, I wonder? Perhaps if we deliver it,\ntheir client will become OUR client. Let's see...
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_011: "To my beloved...Maria..."
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_012: What's wrong, old man? What's with that serious\nlook all of a sudden?
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_013: Something has stolen the grin from your face. What\nis it that troubles you?
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_014: You seem upset. Is there something we should know?
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_015: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_016: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_017: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_018: Oh... It's nothing. Maria's a pretty common name.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_019: But by the scent of the perfume on the package, I'd\nwager she's a woman of elegance, this Maria.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_020: Well, I guess I have no choice but to deliver this in\nperson. She could end up being a valuable customer.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_021: Is that really all it is? You know, I can deliver\nit instead.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_022: *sigh* I suspect that there is more to this.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_023: Your motives strike me as questionable. Do not call\nupon me again when this leads to trouble.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_024: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_025: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_026: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_027: Whoa, now! I've no ulterior motive here, just doing\nmy due diligence as a merchant for the people, see.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_028: I'd appreciate word not getting back to Mandalan\nTrading if possible. Here. The reward as promised.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_030: You have my utmost gratitude! And if you ever need\na favor, you know where to reach me.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_031: Yeah, I'm not gonna get my hopes up. Bye.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_032: If I remember, I shall.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_033: I am aware already. You and I have a prior alliance,\nin case you have forgotten.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_034: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_035: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_036: 
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_037: Maria... Could it be that she's...
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_038: Talimun. The remains of the carriage are secure.\nWe've also removed any trace of our being here.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_039: Excellent work, Ursula. We were able to get all our\ncargo back as well.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_040: In other news, I've received a report regarding the\nOrder of Mithras.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_041: Oh? That's perfect. There's something I wanted to\ndiscuss about that as well.
MID_SCXX_05_03_m01_042: I have this feeling in my gut, Ursula. Feels like\nchange is around the corner... I hope I'm ready for it.